I have a confession to make I have an  addiction my addiction is so compulsive  it interferes with everyday life I'm not  as productive as I want to be I often  find it hard to focus and when people  tell me to stop I simply ignore them I'm  addicted to my smartphone really I'm  addicted to distraction and many of us  here are too on a regular day we unlock  our cell phones more than 120 times per  day I decided to run an experiment to  better understand that egg addiction I  of course used my phone to download an  app called moment and began to track my  usage I apparently unlocked my cell  phone more than a hundred and thirty  times per day that is every nine minutes  what is so gripping that I can't resist  on a good day I'm stalking people on  Facebook I haven't seen since middle  school and on a bad day  I'm reading listicles like ten cute  child stars who grew up to be ugly  why do so many of us feel this  compulsive urge to grab our phone  because our phone is like a slot machine  in Vegas we never know what rewards new  tweet you email in the text message that  child start to an ugly awaits us and the  result a hundred and twenty times per  day we lose our focus don't get me wrong  here I love technology because  technology gives us superpowers  superpowers to see my boyfriend in  Berlin every night and to obtain  information about anything in an instant  or to get into his memory about thoughts  and images so sometimes we do use these  superpowers wisely but most often we  don't and the result 120 times per day  we lose our focus there is a tremendous  cost to this at work in our  relationships and with ourselves at work  we could use these superpowers to do  research or to talk to colleagues  instead we're addicted to distraction  look at me on a typical day I'm sitting  on my computer doing actual work and  quickly check my phone see my messages  take a phone call check my emails on my  phone to then immediately hit refresh on  my computer emails again on days like  these I could have as well stared at the  wall for two hours because according to  research my productivity levels are the  same as after pulling an all-nighter at  work I'm present but absent and maybe  you are too  in our relationships we could use our  superpowers to talk to family and  friends all over the world instead we're  often present but absent a friend of  mine recently said lately my fiance and  I come home and grab dinner we're on our  email still and that makes us feel -  we're together but alone  sometimes I even reject his advances  because I quickly want to finish looking  through my Facebook friends  we've gone now from stonewalling to  phone walling as the relationship expert  John Gottman found it's in our  relationship the number one predictor of  an unhappy union is a lack of  responsiveness and attention in her  relationship my friends often finds  herself present but absent and maybe you  do too let's look at ourselves when  we're alone with our thoughts we could  use their superpowers to capture our  thoughts or think about I read  interesting books and articles instead  we're addicted to distraction and what  would you prefer pain or boredom in an  experiment researchers gave participants  a small electric shock that was so  unpleasant that three-quarters of them  were willing to pay not to experience  that Chuck again then research put those  same participants into a room to sit  alone for 15 minutes  subjects were so uncomfortable being  alone with their own thoughts that they  now shock themselves voluntarily  one outlier press that button a hundred  and ninety times in 15 minutes  shocking I know these participants when  they're alone are absent but present but  absent and maybe you are too  so this is the world we live today I  want to sketch out a new world for you a  world where we can finally make use of  these superpowers to live a more present  life at work in our relationships and  with ourselves at work there is a  concept which is called deep work which  makes you focus without distraction on a  single task and the result increase  productivity improve performance and a  sense of true fulfillment that comes  from craftsmanship I tried it when  writing this talk I went and blocked for  our slots I use my phone for research  but ignored all notification emails and  texts the results I felt productive in a  way I had not felt in a very long time I  felt satisfied with my work and with  myself I felt effective and maybe you  would too let's look at our  relationships my mother helped me see in  different world during Christmas her  simple recipe was a cell phone bowl  during meals and family time we had to  put our cell phone into that bowl today  I'm grateful for this world she created  for us Christmas  truly was endless cookie smells laughter  until we all had tears in her eyes and  my grandmother who came gray and looking  much older than I remembered her leaving  looking rejuvenated with red cheeks and  her beautiful smirk during that time I  felt pure joy and maybe you would too  let's look at ourselves after that  memorable Christmas I was sitting on a  plane back to San Francisco I was  sitting in my seat with no emails and  text to distract myself and my mind went  to how excited I felt flying back into  Silicon Valley that this is what  Florence must have felt like in the  Renaissance  and then started wondering about my  constant struggle to juggle my life in  Germany with my life here for more than  a year I've been debating whether to  stay here or to go home after graduation  I started thinking about how grateful I  was for this wonderful family  and I wondered if they knew how much  this time with them meant to me silent  tears started running down my face and  in that moment I decided that despite of  all the opportunities here I will go  home after graduation because it simply  felt right landing in San Francisco that  morning I felt deeply in touch with  myself what about a world where we don't  feel FOMO because of social media but  because we haven't taken the time to  catch up without mental news feed after  that time in that plane I felt clear and  grounded and maybe you were too so how  can you all deal with your own addiction  to distraction what worked for me is to  take present time and space for work to  take time focused time with my family  and to take that time and space to be  alone with my own thoughts today I'm  finally using those superpowers that  technology gives me to live a more  present life at work in my relationships  and with myself I invite you to do the  same take focus time and space where  distraction is not an option where work  is only work where conversation is only  conversation and where self-reflection  enables you to expand more than you  thought was possible in the philosophers  at Katara's words it is the quality of  our consciousness at a given moment that  shapes our future what do you want this  future to be for you
 

